Delivery: reverse_string.c
The goal of this task is to swap each of the string’s characters, two by two.
In other words, you will swap the first letter with the last one, the second with the second-to-last and so
on.
The function should return a pointer to the first character of the reversed string:
char * reverse_string ( char *str );
For instance:‘
a => a
ab => ba
abc => cba
abcd => dcba
abcde => edcba
abcdef => fedcba
When testing your function you may encounter “Segmentation fault” errors. Either
you’re messing with the pointers in your function or the string given in parameter is read-
only!
Easy way to have read/write string for testing purpose: man 3 strdup .
